Error [E0904]: Can't figure out what `T` should be here
  --> tests/ui/prelude_min_max_clamp_need_one_ordered_type.jet:4:5
    |
  4 |     min((n: Int) -> n, (n: Int) -> n)
    |     ^^^
 Why: Generic calls need enough context to pick a concrete type
 Fix: Pass the type argument explicitly, like `make<Int>()`, or give the value a typed head, like `p :: Pair<Int>{ … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0904

Error [E0112]: `max` wants Int (a whole number) for argument 2, but this is String (text)
  --> tests/ui/prelude_min_max_clamp_need_one_ordered_type.jet:5:12
    |
  5 |     max(1, "two")
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use Int (a whole number) here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0112

Error [E0112]: `clamp` wants Int (a whole number) for argument 2, but this is `Decimal`
  --> tests/ui/prelude_min_max_clamp_need_one_ordered_type.jet:6:14
    |
  6 |     clamp(1, 0.5, 2)
    |              ^^^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use Int (a whole number) here
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0112

Error [E0766]: This call to `min` is missing `b`
  --> tests/ui/prelude_min_max_clamp_need_one_ordered_type.jet:7:5
    |
  7 |     min(1)
    |     ^^^
 Why: `b` has no default, so every call has to supply it
 Fix: Add `b: …` to the call
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0766

Error [E1004]: `core.math` has no item `min`
  --> tests/ui/prelude_min_max_clamp_need_one_ordered_type.jet:8:10
    |
  8 |     math.min(1, 2)
    |          ^^^
 Why: `min` is a prelude name, so every file has it without an import
 Fix: Call it with no module: `min(…)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1004
